A||N||7||Seanh||Where to get this distributor part?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||04-02-2001||05:42 PM||||Ok. When I took my distributor out, I found a broken peice (I didn't even have to break it myself this time!) Anyway, its on a reman distributor. It is that round outer ring, with the points sticking out. It mounts on the distributor housing and goes around the little star shaped peice on the dist. shaft. Mine was broke in two, not completly, but craked and when I removed it, it came apart completly. My question, What is it called, and where can I get it?? Thanks, Also if anyone happens to have one sittin' around...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Thecrewchief1||04-02-2001||05:51 PM||||Its called the dist pickup, you should be able to get it at any bigger parts store or they can order it. Cost should be under $50. A reman dist can cost between $120 to $200 which is your best bet, (I think, take no chances). Read my post above yours, Bill ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||04-02-2001||05:53 PM||||The technical term for that is a reluctor...<BR>I think you can get a new one at NAPA, but be carefull installing the new one.<BR>Make sure the parts don't rub.<BR>Or get a reman dist...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||04-02-2001||07:09 PM||||I would get a reman distributor, but I just replaced mine last year for $180. I checked out at GM parts a few min ago, and they don't just sell it by itself, it comes with the pickup coil, and the metal mounting bracket under it, they want $56 for it! I can't believe this little $2 worth of metal is going to cost me that much. This sucks! Maybe I should just glue my old one and call it good?||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||04-03-2001||12:11 AM||||Go to advance auto, Napa, Auto Zone,Pep Boys,<BR>Or any major auto parts store. If you have a advance auto parts store, I think they are the best. Anytime they tell you at GM the part is $56.00 dollars, then it will cost you about half this at these other stores.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||04-03-2001||08:07 AM||||Since the reluctor is not a wear item why not hit the junk yard for a used distributor?  It may be in better shape than yours or you could at least cannibalize it for parts.<P>I'd suggest dismantling the distributor since you have it out anyway and clean up the shaft.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||04-03-2001||07:36 PM||||Mine is a reman job, put in by GM last year. Sorry, I have no junkyards in Hicktown, NE here. If anyone is at a junkyard please look for one, or if you have a working distributor email me about how much you would sell it for. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||04-03-2001||08:00 PM||||Seanh, I may have one. I,ll check in the morning. One of my cars had three old distributor bodys in the trunk. If I can salvage one I,ll send it to you. I,d check now but it,s raining big time and has been all day.||||reg||1
